<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prussian coup of 1932</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1932</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Preußenschlag</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Prussian coup of 20 July 1932, the Preußenschlag, was the removal of the Social Democratic-led government of the Free State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> by Chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-von-papen">Franz von Papen</a>, using an emergency decree of President Hindenburg. Papen took control as Reich commissioner for Prussia, removing a key defender of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a> and easing the Nazi seizure of power. The Constitutional Court ruled it partly unlawful in October 1932.</p></div>
